ported leadership at term 2 (index 17, with the incumbent state outside the cited subset). Controls in the same receipt hold: the local-type message is still rejected with ErrStepLocalMsg (index 3), the under-lease pre-vote is not granted in either stream (indices 4 and 10), and the local API produces the same lead transition the network path should not reach (index 2). The mechanism is the one in the main account: the type is missing from isLocalMsg although only the local ForgetLeader APIs produce it, and the peer-form message carries no term so Step treats it as local and skips term checks.\\\",\n  \\\"counterevidence\\\":[\\\"The competing explanation that this follower grants pre-votes and votes regardless of its leader is excluded by the under-lease controls in the same receipt (indices 4 and 10).\\\",\\\"The change is per-message and reversible: the next genuine leader heartbeat restored the context and the same pre-vote was ignored again (indices 7 and 8).\\\"],\n  \\\"limitations\\\":[\\\"Single process with hand-delivered messages and one tick configuration; the window bound is in ticks, not wall-clock time.\\\",\\\"The quorum scenario uses one voter plus the candidate, so the quorum size itself was not varied.\\\",\\\"ReadOnlyLeaseBased configurations still refuse the message, so this does not bear on lease-based reads.\\\"]}]}\njson.dump(upd,open('draft/update.json','w'),indent=1,ensure_ascii=False)\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_00-04-05-etcd_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -2\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
